account pii retention
=====================

billing/accounts/*.rec is the account master and holds customer pii: CUST_NM,
TAX_ID and SVC_ADDR. data/accounts.csv is a mirror of it, and data/locations.csv
carries the customer name for each serviceable location.

policy (billing/retention.h)

  open account      pii kept, it is needed to bill.
  closed account    STATUS=CLOSED and CLOSED_DT= go on the record. the whole
                    record is kept for RETENTION_YEARS (6) after CLOSED_DT so
                    invoices can be reissued and audited.
  erasure request   a closed account is anonymized straight away: CUST_NM
                    becomes REDACTED, TAX_ID and SVC_ADDR are blanked, and
                    ANONYMIZED_DT= is stamped. billing ref, province, plan and
                    balances stay, so the invoice still totals the same. an
                    open account has to be closed first.
  retention expiry  the record is purged: the .rec is deleted, its row is
                    dropped from data/accounts.csv and the customer name is
                    replaced with REDACTED on data/locations.csv (unless
                    another account that still holds pii goes by that name).

six years follows the CRA books and records period. finance owns the number,
change RETENTION_YEARS if it moves.

tool, dry run unless --apply

  bin/account-retention close BEACON-004417 --on 2026-09-30 --apply
  bin/account-retention anonymize BEACON-004417 --on 2026-10-01 --apply
  bin/account-retention report
  bin/account-retention sweep --as-of 2026-10-01 [--apply]
  make retention-sweep            dry run sweep as of today

  --accounts DIR --accounts-csv PATH --locations PATH point it at another store.
  sweep --apply is meant to run monthly after the billing run.

derived outputs

  billing-run --json (reconciliation feed) and invoice-api build their output
  from the .rec on every request and keep no copy, so an anonymized or purged
  record drops out of them on the next run. copies already sent downstream
  (vantage-telco parity runs, finance exports) are the receiver's to delete.
  vantage-telco tools/fixtures/generate_fixtures.py rewrites billing/accounts/
  and data/accounts.csv from scratch, closures and anonymizations included.

what this does not cover

  git history       a deleted or rewritten record is still in old commits.
                    after an erasure or purge lands, a repo admin has to
                    rewrite history, e.g.
                      git filter-repo --invert-paths --path billing/accounts/<ACCT_ID>.rec
                    and for the csv mirrors use --replace-text with the old
                    values, then force push, ask github support to drop cached
                    views and pull refs, and have everyone re-clone.
  backups           snapshots and backups of this repo or of the hosts that
                    run billing keep their copy until they age out. their
                    retention must not be longer than RETENTION_YEARS.
